Hi Melissa,

Following our call yesterday, I understand Robert decided to retain the six-m=
onth interval for CE-Reader-2. The four in-range visits included two suppleme=
ntal checks, so they do not establish performance over a full twelve months w=
ithout calibration. The increase in active use is a separate consideration su=
pporting the decision to keep the current cadence.

I have booked April 22, 2026, 09:30=E2=80=9311:30 EDT for the scheduled servi=
ce and calibration. The appointment notice is attached. Please reserve the re=
ader and leave the service-side bench and working clearance clear. The window=
 is for the visit; we will confirm the actual release time on April 22 when t=
he work is complete and the reader is handed back.

Best,
Christopher Medina
Mason Laboratory Maintenance

